Give swaynag's no-op Wayland listeners their callback prototypes

swaynag fills eleven Wayland listener slots with one unprototyped
function:

    static void nop() {
    	// Intentionally left blank
    }

libwayland calls each slot with the arguments of its event, so the
same function is called as, for example,

    void (*)(void *, struct wl_output *)               wl_output.done
    void (*)(void *, struct wl_seat *, const char *)   wl_seat.name

Calling a function through a pointer to an incompatible function type
is undefined behavior (C11 6.3.2.3p8). Native calling conventions happen
to tolerate the extra arguments, but a WebAssembly indirect call checks
the callee's signature and traps: swaynag died with "null function or
function signature mismatch" in its startup roundtrip, before it
mapped its bar. The same code fails under control-flow-integrity
checking (clang -fsanitize=cfi-icall) on native targets.

Replace nop with one empty function per slot, each with the prototype
of its event, as swaybar already does.

This is a portability fix, not a Kandelo adaptation: nothing here is
specific to one platform.

